{"name":"Espresso","hex":"#4e312d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"espresso","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A concentrated coffee beverage brewed by forcing hot water under high pressure through finely ground coffee.","A drink that includes espresso as an ingredient."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/espresso"}],"entries":[{"title":"Espresso","blocks":[{"text":"Espresso is a concentrated form of coffee produced by forcing hot water under high pressure through finely ground coffee beans. Originating in Italy, espresso has become one of the most popular coffee-brewing methods worldwide. It is characterized by its small serving size, typically 25–30 ml, and its distinctive layers: a dark body topped with a lighter-colored foam called \"crema\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Tazzina_di_caff%C3%A8_a_Ventimiglia.jpg/330px-Tazzina_di_caff%C3%A8_a_Ventimiglia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Espresso"},{"title":"Espresso (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Espresso\" is a song by American singer Sabrina Carpenter from her sixth studio album, Short n' Sweet (2024). Island Records released it on April 11, 2024, as the album's lead single. It was written by Carpenter herself along with Amy Allen, Steph Jones, and its producer Julian Bunetta. A combination of pop, funk, and dance with other subgenres, the song contains lyrics about self-confidence."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/71/Espresso_-_Sabrina_Carpenter.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Espresso_(song)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Victoria_Arduino%2C_1922.jpg/500px-Victoria_Arduino%2C_1922.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Victoria_Arduino%2C_1922.jpg/1280px-Victoria_Arduino%2C_1922.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Victoria_Arduino%2C_1922.jpg/500px-Victoria_Arduino%2C_1922.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A man pulls an espresso while leaning out of a train in a 1922 advertisement for a \"caffé espresso\" machine. The imagery references the shared associations of speed and steam, as well as name: in Italy, a class of trains is called \"espresso\".[11]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVictoria_Arduino%2C_1922.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Angelo-moriondo-portrait-espresso-machine-inventor.jpg/330px-Angelo-moriondo-portrait-espresso-machine-inventor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Angelo-moriondo-portrait-espresso-machine-inventor.jpg/330px-Angelo-moriondo-portrait-espresso-machine-inventor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAngelo-moriondo-portrait-espresso-machine-inventor.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Espresso-machine-first-patent-angelo-moriondo.jpg/500px-Espresso-machine-first-patent-angelo-moriondo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Espresso-machine-first-patent-angelo-moriondo.jpg/500px-Espresso-machine-first-patent-angelo-moriondo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEspresso-machine-first-patent-angelo-moriondo.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Bezzera_%26_caff%C3%A